choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 662}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "One fifth of white women aged 65 have osteoporosis ……………………", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 747}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Certain number of aspects is considered before treating osteoporosis.\n……………….", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 813}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "The major side effect of bisphosphonates. …………………", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 903}, {"number": 7, "prompt": "The incidence of fractures associated with osteoporosis is increasing with\nthe aging of population. …………….", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 959}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "Which is the most prevalent bone disease in the world?\n………………………………", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1274}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What are the two hormones which help in maintaining bone mass in men?\n…………………………………..", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1355}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Which medication is used to reduce the rate of broken bone?\n…………………………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "Which test is performed to diagnose osteoporosis?\n……………………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 88}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What are the two types of osteoporosis?\n…………………………………", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 168}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "What is the percentage of Caucasian women, who are expected to have\nosteoporosis related fracture in their lives?\n……………………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 236}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "What is the estimated cost involved to treat osteoporosis annually in the US?\n……………………………………...", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 385}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "Formation of new bone is called as ………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 692}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "The risk of osteoporosis increases with ………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 743}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "Consumption of anticoagulants may affects …………………. and\nmetabolism", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 799}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Hot flushes, leg cramps and blood clots are the side effects of\n………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 878}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "……………………. million osteoporotic fractures are noted with the aging\nof population every year.", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 964}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "Patients with osteoporosis should maintain sufficient levels of\n……………………", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1069}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [22, 23]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f-p8", "label": "Part B · Reading 27.pdf", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "pages": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "questions": [{"number": 6, "prompt": "What should be considered while selecting analgesics?\na. Its various effects on peripheral and central nervous system.\nb. The different types and their respective effects.\nc. Their severity and response to other medication\n6.ANALGESICS\nAn analgesic or painkiller is any member of the group of drugs used to achieve\nanalgesia, relief from pain. Analgesic drugs act in various ways on the peripheral\nand central nervous systems. They are distinct from anesthetics, which temporarily\naffect, and in some instances completely eliminate, sensation. Analgesics include\nparacetamol (known in North America as acetaminophen or simply APAP), the\nnonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) such as the salicylates, and opioid\ndrugs such as morphine and oxycodone. When choosing analgesics, the severity\nand response to other medication determines the choice of agent; the World Health\nOrganization (WHO) pain ladder specifies mild analgesics as its first step.", "sourcePage": 13, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 23}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [22, 23]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f-p14", "label": "Part C · Reading 27.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "pages": [14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21], "questions": [{"number": 14, "prompt": "The term ‘Idiopathic’ in the passage 1 indicates?\nA. the disease which occurs randomly without family history or gender\nB. when the route cause of a disease is unknown.\nC. the disease which occurs in an ideal way\nD. The disease which occurs all of a sudden causing death.", "sourcePage": 17, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 319, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 23}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Which one of these is common in thyroid diseases?\nA. loss of appetite\nB. decreased metabolism\nC. tiredness\nD. none of the above", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 559, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 23}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "According to the information given, “Grave’s disease” occurs more commonly\nin\nA. men\nB. women\nC. children\nD. adult women", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 819, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 23}}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "‘graves disease’ in paragraph 6 is?\nA. condition in which too much thyroid harmone is produced due to some\nantibodies in the blood\nB. over production of thyroid hormone due to the over activity of immature\nthyroid gland\nC. unconditional production of TSH\nD. condition in which less thyroid harmone secreated by entire thyroid gland", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 118, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 23}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752", "filename": "Reading 27.pdf", "sha256": "b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b9d3c47ea8503c2f8752d983e34df2ff0ccdd76c8f5adee44d5d447f8d501b0e.json", "format": "pdf", 